<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sabha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sebha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sabha is the largest city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> region in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, an oasis town on the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. Under Italian rule it was a military post, and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it served as the centre of the French-administered territory of Fezzan. In the independent Kingdom of Libya it was the capital of Fezzan province, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muammar-gaddafi">Muammar Gaddafi</a> went to school there.</p></div>
